+**The per-line check** (prototype, `SHAPE_CHECK`; research/free-shape/round2/STEP3.md). A model error the refinement does not carry (an amorphous hump, a size distribution, an impurity, air scatter, texture) can be read as shape: with the exact line, all four unbounded extents of the 77 screening runs and both spheres that kept a shape had one. So every fit the search returns (the shape kept, or the isotropic one) is checked line by line:
+
+- **Segments.** The range is cut into one segment per line, or per group of lines that overlap: the phase's reflections at their Kα centroids, a line within max(0.3°, the mean FWHM of it and the group's last) joining the group, the cuts at the midpoints.
+- **Two statistics** of the residuals r = √w (y − y_c), each made family-wise (Bonferroni) over the pattern: the worst segment's χ² (its upper tail as a normal deviate, Wilson–Hilferty), and the worst sum of r over 1° (two-sided; a line's intensity misfit, as texture makes, shows there and may not in its χ²_ν).
+- **The flag** fires when either exceeds z = 3.09 (p = 0.001 each). On the screening runs it fired on none of the 39 clean rows (the worst 2.08) and on 29 of the 38 with an error, 14 of the 15 whose result the error had spoiled. Round 1's worst segment χ²_ν > 1.25 fired on 2 clean rows and 23 error rows.
+- **The jackknife over lines**, where it fires (`bodyShapeOf`): the segments in at most 20 contiguous groups, each weighted 0 in turn and the fit refined from itself (4 iterations, its own free parameters: a held frame stays held). Each dimension gets D·e^(±2 sd) (`jackLo`, `jackHi`) and each axis 2·rms turn (`jackTurn`) beside its esds; the check is `misfit`. On the 24 flagged truths with an error it covered 51 of 56 extents where the esds alone covered 28, at 0.24× the fit's evaluations.
+- **The keep test again** (`retest`, off): without the worst flagged segments, at most a third of them. On the screening runs it rejected 1 of the 2 false shapes and 4 of the 13 shapes an error had spoiled, and no shape that was read well; the unbounded extents stayed.
+- **What it cannot do.** Shapes a size distribution or texture makes on a sphere are spread over every line and stay (their anisotropy is 7–13 jackknife sd). A misfit that leaves no residual (a size distribution taken up whole by a held spheroid, χ²_ν 1.003) goes unseen.
+
+**The minima stage** (prototype, `SHAPE_MINIMA`; research/free-shape/round2/STEP4.md). The search returns one fit, but near-equivalent minima are common: on round 2's 77 screening runs 24 of the 68 kept shapes have another within Δ* of the lowest. Where the search keeps a body's shape, every true minimum is refined to the same level and each parameter gets two errors, kept apart:
+
+- **The ends.** Every refinement end of the search (brief trials, full refinements, the exact faces' fit, the held frames) within 30 χ²_ν of the lowest, one of each minimum (the class's operations and the body's own relabellings; widths within 10 %, axes within 5°), at most 6, the lowest first.
+- **Refined to the same level.** Exact faces, central differences, the orientation free, the covariance at the end; then turned by ±0.02 rad about the softest turn (the turns' covariance's largest-variance direction; at a symmetric orientation about every turn) and refined again, the lower kept while it gains, at most 10 rounds. No random number is left: with the stage on, the search's polish and its held fit's refit, each from a random 0.02 rad turn that decided the free minimum in flat valleys (up to 7.5 χ²_ν), are not made.
+- **Merged again** within each other's local error (2σ, floored at 2 % and 1°, angles capped at 10°). The lowest free minimum replaces the search's free fit when lower, and a held frame is tested against it again.
+- **The true minima** lie within Δ* = 16 χ²_ν of the lowest, 25 where the per-line check fired: the 5 % point of a parametric bootstrap on tuning rows, the flips read against the data's Δ (round 1's model of the replicas, N(δ, 4δ + c), gives c 8.5 and 12.6 again, but under-predicts the flips beyond 12.5: 10 % of 40 against 2 %; with a model error the competitor still wins 12–17 % beyond 12.5).
+- **Two errors.** The local one: the curvature's for the dimensions (Desd), the profile's for the angles (esdAngle, §10.11). The second one: the spread over the true minima, each paired with the reported fit: each dimension's range (betweenLo–betweenHi) and each axis's largest angle (betweenDeg). One minimum within Δ* means no second error: the shape is unique (minima.unique). The report joins them as one 95 % interval, lo–hi: the hull of D·e^(±2κσ) (κ = 1.2), the minima's range and, where the check fired, the jackknife's; each axis's radius is the largest of 2·esdAngle, betweenDeg and jackTurn. κ: the curvature's σ is right against noise (bootstrap replicas 0.97 σ rms), but the truth lies 1.21 σ rms off on the clean rows; with κ 1.2 the local interval covers 77 of their 82 dimensions, the combined one 78 (95 %) at a median half-width of 3.1 %; the principal axes 25 and 29 of 32. Where the check fired the jackknife carries most of it: 51 of 56 dimensions with it, 31 without.
+- **Directions as sets.** A box's edges not told apart, and a square box's two sides, give their directions as an unordered set with the error of the turn about the set's normal (sets); a turn is lost only where it is a true symmetry of the solid (an ellipsoid's or an elliptic section's equal pair, a body of revolution).
